# ---- sys-1w0hoy ask 3: audit widened to ALL text files (was a suffix
# whitelist; estate tokens rode in .yml/.txt/extensionless seat/label wording).
# First hits the widened audit fires, classified per docs/PUBLISH-SCRUB.md: ----
# Upstream repo pin: the PR-tag audit resolves `(open PR #NN)` doc tags against
# the PARENT repo (upstream numbering); the owner handle in the repo slug is
# load-bearing data — resolving against the fork would fail closed on wrong
# numbers (ci.yml's own comment says so). GUARD line-anchored to the audit
# invocation, NOT file-wide, so a future stray token in ci.yml still fires.
regex:pr_tag_audit\.py --repo jacobhausler/
# Copyright attribution to the upstream owner is the license; GUARD (load-
# bearing identity, same class as the PR-author-credit regex guards).
LICENSE
# The committed scrub-grep list quotes the banned vocabulary because it IS the
# ban — self-referential GUARD, exactly scripts/.scrub-guards' own exemption.
scripts/scrub-list.txt
# Ratelimit-window fake child: the banner quotes the model alias verbatim
# because the runner's give-up error must quote it back byte-for-byte — the
# same GUARD class as tests/fake_hermes.py / tests/test_ratelimit_54.py.
tests/fake-b1
# ---- #580 take-over (pre-existing red, sys-asvm0c feed lane): the pr-feed
# workflow's CHANNEL line routes the PR-open digest to the estate's private
# Discord feed — the routing id IS the integration's load-bearing config,
# neutralizing it ships a broken feed (same load-bearing-routing class as the
# pr-compliance citation rows). Anchored by the CHANNEL token + quoted digits,
# not by file:LINE (est-867 lesson), so a stray non-id private string in
# pr-feed.yml still fires. FULL-LINE-ANCHORED (#580 adversary R9-narrow): the
# exemption covers ONLY a pure routing assignment line — a line that carries
# this shape plus any other content (e.g. a second forbidden token appended)
# still fires the audit. GUARD, per docs/PUBLISH-SCRUB.md / AGENTS.md rule 4.
regex:^\s*CHANNEL:\s*"[0-9]{17,20}"\s*$

